{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121549","id":4085633314,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7zhdEi","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121549","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121549.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121549.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121549","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121549/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121549/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121549/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/efe1cd69dacf164e1c996dad0cc1b501e101b45f","number":121549,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `DirAccessWindows::list_dir_begin()` for listing contents of root dirs of virtual drives","user":{"login":"jspohr","id":1578023,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzgwMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1578023?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr","html_url":"https://github.com/jspohr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jspohr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe FileDialog on Windows doesn't show any files for the root directory of drives that are mapped to a directory using `subst`.\r\n\r\nTo reproduce, map a directory (not a drive) to a new drive letter, like this:\r\n`subst X: C:\\Windows`\r\nStart Godot, and in the Project Manager click \"Import\" and select the X: drive - it will show up empty.\r\n\r\nWhat's the bug in the current code?\r\n`DirAccessWindows::list_dir_begin` appends a `\\*` to the `current_dir`. If, and only if, `current_dir` is the root of a drive, it ends with a backslash, like this: `\\\\?\\X:\\`. Appending `\\*` to that creates a double backslash, and the path that is passed to `FindFirstFileExW` will be `\\\\?\\X:\\\\*`.\r\nNow, the `\\\\?\\` prefix is a well-known Win32 hack to allow long filenames, but as a side-effect, it disables path normalization. This means that the double backslash between the colon and the asterisk is not removed: https://projectzero.google/2016/02/the-definitive-guide-on-win32-to-nt.html\r\n\r\nWhy does the double backslash break listing the contents of subst-ed drives, but not physical drives? The device driver internally handles a double backslash that directly follows the drive letter plus colon. `subst`, on the other hand, just replaces the drive letter with the path the drive is mapped to, and ends up with that path followed by a double backslash, which is invalid if not normalized. The result is `FindFirstFileExW` will return  `INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE`.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis is my first contribution, let me know of any details I may have missed! Thank you\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":